.TH "libnvme" 9 "enum nvme_personality_identifier" "October 2026" "API Manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
enum nvme_personality_identifier \- Personality Identifier List
.SH SYNOPSIS
enum nvme_personality_identifier {
.br
.BI "    NVME_PERID_MFG_DEFAULT"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_PERID_SECURITY"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_PERID_LOCKDOWN_PERSISTENCE"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_PERID_REVERT_MFG_SETTINGS"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_PERID_ALL"

};
.SH Constants
.IP "NVME_PERID_MFG_DEFAULT" 12
Manufacturing Default Personality
.IP "NVME_PERID_SECURITY" 12
Security Personality
.IP "NVME_PERID_LOCKDOWN_PERSISTENCE" 12
Lockdown Persistence Personality, see
\fIenum nvme_lockdown_persistence_cdw11\fP
and \fIenum
nvme_lockdown_persistence_cqe_dw1\fP
.IP "NVME_PERID_REVERT_MFG_SETTINGS" 12
Revert to Subsystem Manufacturing
Settings Personality: reverts all
supported Features (other than CDP
itself), restorable log pages, and
vendor specific settings to their
manufacturing default content for the
current active firmware image. Uses no
data buffer; requires an NVM Subsystem
Reset (see \fIenum
nvme_personality_mrstt\fP) to take effect.
.IP "NVME_PERID_ALL" 12
All Personalities
